Ways a document is lost:
- C does not attempt it (deadline, elapsed time, breaker or allowance; a refusal also makes the comparison INCOMPLETE);
- C returns unsupported_input;
- an alias is counted twice;
- the adapter's handling of F019;
- the rolling limit of 60 requests per project per day across tracks (4-5 run-set documents per project on average, up to 10, at up to 8 requests each).
Binomial: per-document loss of 10%/20%/30% gives P(matched < 12) of 1.7%/20%/55%. Earlier runs ended on breakers (four-arm final 234/688, L1 breaker). Neither PREPARATION-REPORT discusses this.

